μ≡{"learn.component":"photon/device.go, photon/loopback.go, photon/host.go (leaseThisLaptop), rinkvt-photon leases","learn.contract":"every laptop keeps one 127.x.y.z address for good: the address is leased to the laptop's device key, pinned in its device file, and asked for in every lease table the laptop meets; a table grants it unless another laptop holds it there, so no table ever gives one address to two laptops; a fleet register that every laptop shares makes the addresses unique everywhere; a lease is written, synced and sealed before the address is used","learn.device_key":"device: followed by the first 32 hex digits of HMAC-SHA-256 with the key 'RINK-VT device 1' over the trimmed, lower-cased machine identifier; the identifier itself is never stored; a computer without one gets a random 128-bit key","learn.machine_identifier":{"windows":"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\MachineGuid","macos":"IOPlatformUUID","linux":"/etc/machine-id or /var/lib/dbus/machine-id"},"learn.device_file":{"windows":"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\RINK-VT\\device.json","macos":"~/Library/Application Support/RINK-VT/device.json","linux":"$XDG_DATA_HOME/rink-vt/device.json","override":"RINKVT_DEVICE_FILE or --device-file"},"learn.pool":"127.16.0.0/12","learn.capacity":1040384,"learn.slot":"the first 16 hex digits of SHA-256('RINK-VT loopback 1' NUL key), modulo the capacity; then linear probing over host addresses .1 to .254","learn.keys":"a device key; or, as the reference edition keys its clients, the canonical text of an IP address (RFC 5952; an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address is its IPv4 address)","learn.file_format":"a header line '# RINK-VT loopback leases · format 2 · pool P · ipv6 /N', then one line per lease: address, key, time and a 16-digit seal; a format 1 table (IP keys only) is read, and upgraded once, every line kept, when it receives a device key","learn.fleet_register":"a lease table on a share or a removable disk that every laptop of a club or league uses (--fleet, remembered once given); never created where its folder is missing; when it cannot be reached, the pinned address is used","learn.refusals":["an edited or damaged line","a second lease for one key or one address","a pool or IPv6 prefix other than the file's","a device key in a format 1 table","a full pool"],"learn.ja_contract":"contracts/ja/rinkvt_loopback.ja","learn.maturity":"OPERATIONAL","learn.evidence":["photon/loopback_test.go","photon/device_test.go","photon/browser_test.go"]},
